abstract: >-
  Evidence for data-career decisions in Austria, in four layers. Layer 1 (employer demand): a one-day
  snapshot (2026-09-16) of open data-role job advertisements collected from five posting sources plus the
  AMS JobBarometer yearly series 2020-2025 and Eurostat job-vacancy statistics, normalised with transparent
  rule-based taxonomies (720 core postings). Layer 2 (observed candidate supply): public GitHub profiles and
  repositories of Austria-located accounts collected through the documented GitHub API, the Stack Overflow
  Developer Survey 2025 (ODbL) and Eurostat graduate and employment series. Layer 3 (demand × supply):
  skill-by-skill comparison of what employers ask for with what candidates demonstrate. Layer V (visual
  decision layer): decision questions each answered by one figure. The public repository contains the
  author's code, methodology, configuration, aggregated tables, figures and JSON summaries, and the openly
  licensed Eurostat raw data; posting collectors, source records, advertisement texts and individual-level
  candidate records are retained privately.
